# Everything the build does not need. Without this the context includes
# target/ -- hundreds of megabytes of classes, jars and JaCoCo data -- which is
# uploaded to the daemon on every build and then thrown away.
target/
*.log

# Profile configuration that has no business in a production image.
#
# application-local.yaml is the real one: gitignored, holds live credentials,
# and an image carrying it would put them wherever the image goes.
#
# The .example templates hold only placeholders, so they leak nothing -- they
# are excluded because they are dead weight that reads like configuration, and
# because the rule "no profile files in the image" is easier to hold than "no
# profile files except the harmless ones".
#
# application-test.yaml is the test profile. It is in src/main/resources, so
# Maven packages it into the jar; excluding it here keeps it out. It is the one
# with teeth: left in the image, a mistyped SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE could
# activate a configuration written for a throwaway database.
src/main/resources/application-local.yaml
src/main/resources/application-test.yaml
src/main/resources/*.example
